WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:16.632
Early the next morning, the doctor climbed up from Dorfli with Peter and the goats.

2
00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:21.565
When they reached the hut, Heidi was waiting for them with Daisy and Dusky.

3
00:00:21.566 --> 00:00:25.248
"Coming up today?" asked Peter as usual.

4
00:00:25.249 --> 00:00:29.917
"Yes. The doctor is coming too," she replied.

5
00:00:29.918 --> 00:00:33.097
Peter glanced sideways at the doctor.

6
00:00:33.098 --> 00:00:40.594
Then, Grandfather came out, said good morning to the doctor, and hung a bag of food over Peter's shoulder.

7
00:00:40.595 --> 00:00:48.100
It was a little heavier than usual, and Peter grinned at the thought of what might be inside.

8
00:00:48.101 --> 00:00:50.724
They set off up the mountain.

9
00:00:50.725 --> 00:00:54.645
The goats surrounded Heidi until she waved them ahead.

10
00:00:54.646 --> 00:00:57.783
"Run along now," she said.

11
00:00:57.784 --> 00:01:00.740
"I want to walk with the doctor."

12
00:01:00.741 --> 00:01:08.452
Heidi happily chatted to the doctor about the goats and the flowers she wanted to show him.

13
00:01:08.453 --> 00:01:17.651
At a spot where they could look down on the distant valley and up to the snow sparkling on the mountain above, they sat down.

14
00:01:17.652 --> 00:01:22.374
The goat-bells tinkled pleasantly as the herd moved about.

15
00:01:22.375 --> 00:01:27.049
Heidi looked at the doctor to see if he was enjoying the scene.

16
00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:30.903
He could tell from her eyes what was on her mind.

17
00:01:30.904 --> 00:01:35.364
"Yes, Heidi, it's very beautiful," he said.

18
00:01:35.365 --> 00:01:42.186
He thought for a little about his daughter, who had died, and then asked, almost to himself,

19
00:01:42.187 --> 00:01:47.097
"Can a heart forget sorrow and be happy, even here?"

20
00:01:47.098 --> 00:01:53.215
"No one is sad here," Heidi answered. "Only in Frankfurt."

21
00:01:53.216 --> 00:01:56.485
A thoughtful expression crossed his face.

22
00:01:56.486 --> 00:02:02.804
"But what if you can't leave all the sadness behind in Frankfurt?" he said.

23
00:02:02.805 --> 00:02:09.558
"When there is nothing you can do," Heidi said confidently, "tell God."

24
00:02:09.559 --> 00:02:13.149
"Those are good words," said the doctor.

25
00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:21.911
"Can you understand that, even up here, sorrow can cast a shadow so that you can't really see all the beauty?"

26
00:02:21.912 --> 00:02:29.770
Heidi thought about his words, and they reminded her that Grannie would never see the sunlight or the mountains.

27
00:02:29.771 --> 00:02:34.576
Then, she said, "I can tell you one of Grannie's prayers.

28
00:02:34.577 --> 00:02:39.250
She says they always bring light to her heart."

29
00:02:39.251 --> 00:02:46.084
The doctor nodded, so Heidi clasped her hands together and recited Grannie's favorite prayer.

30
00:02:46.085 --> 00:02:51.901
She knew it well because Grannie always asked her to read it three times over.

31
00:02:51.902 --> 00:02:55.152
She ended with the last verse:

32
00:02:55.153 --> 00:02:58.264
To God confide your cares,

33
00:02:58.265 --> 00:03:01.377
On Him your burden cast,

34
00:03:01.378 --> 00:03:04.570
He hears your every prayer,

35
00:03:04.571 --> 00:03:08.168
And sends relief at last.

36
00:03:08.169 --> 00:03:11.748
The doctor listened with his eyes closed.

37
00:03:11.749 --> 00:03:19.085
It was the same verse that his mother often sang to him as a boy, and it cheered his heart greatly.

38
00:03:19.086 --> 00:03:22.041
He patted Heidi's hand and said,

39
00:03:22.042 --> 00:03:25.679
"Thank you, Heidi. We'll come up here again."

40
00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.971
All of this was not to Peter's liking.

41
00:03:28.972 --> 00:03:37.815
This was the first day in weeks that Heidi had come up the mountain, and now, she was sitting with the doctor the whole time.

42
00:03:37.816 --> 00:03:40.830
He kicked at the grass and scowled.

43
00:03:40.831 --> 00:03:48.778
At midday, when the sun was overhead, he ran up to them and shouted loudly, "Dinner time!"

44
00:03:48.779 --> 00:03:53.624
The doctor laughed, and they opened up the bag with the food.

45
00:03:53.625 --> 00:04:03.690
Heidi and the doctor shared most of their lunch with Peter, including a large, hearty sausage that Grandfather had included.

46
00:04:03.691 --> 00:04:10.435
For the rest of the month, the doctor often went for long walks with Grandfather in the clear air.

47
00:04:10.436 --> 00:04:14.628
He enjoyed just as much his trips up the mountain with Heidi.

48
00:04:14.629 --> 00:04:18.863
On his last day, he thanked them both.

49
00:04:18.864 --> 00:04:23.322
Heidi waved as he headed down to Dorfli one last time.

50
00:04:23.323 --> 00:04:26.895
The doctor turned for a final look and thought,

51
00:04:26.896 --> 00:04:30.428
"This is certainly a wonderful place for healing.

52
00:04:30.429 --> 00:04:37.246
Life seems really worth living again."
